  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The combination – pass, skate and shoot",
  "description": "Two lines along one board: A close to the net with the pucks and B further out. A passes to B, who receives and passes back. B then skates backwards down to the lower cone, turns and heads for the net. A carries the puck around behind the net and, at the post, passes to B coming in, then steps in as a defender. B shoots.\n\nThe drill uses one zone, so another drill can run in the other. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the ice, and show with your stick where you want the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B: skate backwards in a low stance and turn quickly with a crossover."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: look up at the post before you pass."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
